The '''Kubaz''' were an [[insectoid]] [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] that were [[Homeworld|native]] to the [[planet]] [[Kubindi]]. They lived on a [[diet]] of [[insect]]s, using their long [[Nose|snout]] to snatch their prey from inside hives. This did not make them very popular with sentient [[insectoid]] species, such as the [[Geonosian]]s,<ref name="Alien Archive">''[[Star Wars: Alien Archive]]''</ref> despite the Kubaz themselves being descended from insects.<ref name="The Secrets of Long Snoot" /> They had dark skin, long snouts, and sensitive [[eye]]sight causing them to require protective eyewear.<ref name="Alien Archive" /> On the whole, their appearance resembled<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> that of the [[northern Mustafarian]]s.<ref name="Absolutely Everything You Need to Know">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> Kubaz were unable to pronounce the phonemes of [[Galactic Basic Standard]], and [[Kubazian|their]] [[language]] was made of whirring syllables.<ref name="DB Kubaz" />

At one time, the Kubaz wrote in a script which, by the [[High Republic Era]], was remembered as [[Ancient Kubaz]].<ref name="Into the Dark">''[[The High Republic: Into the Dark]]''</ref> The [[Galactic Empire]] [[Blockade of Kubindi|conquered]] the Kubaz species after claiming they could be allies. The Empire [[Slavery|enslaved]] Kubaz and sought to brainwash others to make them into [[Spy|spies]].<ref name="The Secrets of Long Snoot" />

==Kubaz in the galaxy==
{{Quote|Look, I'm not bigoted or nothing, but the Kubaz are a trash species.|[[Sardis Ramsin]] displays anti-Kubaz [[xenophobia]]|<ref name="Born in the Storm">{{StoryCite|story=Born in the Storm|book=From a Certain Point of View}}</ref>}}
[[File:KubazCourier-CaM.png|thumb|left|180px|A Kubaz courier]]
One member of this species was [[Garindan ezz Zavor]], an informant who worked for the highest bidder.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> He had escaped Imperial brainwashing with his freewill intact and sought to liberate his species, even if it meant taking jobs from the Empire in the meantime.<ref name="The Secrets of Long Snoot" /> Another was [[Ooblamon]], a junk dealer from [[Taris]] who claimed to have recovered the [[Darth Vader's lightsaber|red-bladed lightsaber]] that had belonged to [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]].<ref name="Aftermath">[[Aftermath (novel)|''Aftermath'']]</ref> Another Kubaz was [[Rikard Lovas]], a male banker who regularly conducted business on the planet [[Jakku]] that fell into gambling debts owed to the [[Irving Boys]].<ref name="High Noon on Jakku">{{StoryCite|story=High Noon on Jakku|book=Tales from a Galaxy Far, Far Away: Aliens: Volume I}}</ref>

A Kubaz participated in the [[Ferrix Riot|Rix Road riot]] in [[5 BBY]] on [[Ferrix]].<ref name="Rix Road">{{Andor|Rix Road (episode)}}</ref> Another member of the Kubaz worked as a [[Unidentified Kubaz ferryman|ferryman]] on the [[Water|ice]] planet [[Pagodon]] around [[9 ABY]].<ref name="Mando1">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 1: The Mandalorian}}</ref> Another was a [[Unidentified Kubaz bounty hunter|bounty hunter]] who was after [[Din Grogu|Grogu]] on [[Sorgan]].<ref name="Chapter 4">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 4: Sanctuary}}</ref> The Kubaz [[Glikkin]] arose to become a [[Master Thief|master thief]] and [[Hunter (Grand Arena)|competitor]] in the [[Hunters of the Outer Rim]]. Glikkin hailed from the lower levels of the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]], something that he swore never to forget.<ref name="Hunters">''[[Star Wars: Hunters]]''</ref>

